{% comment %}
  sections/home-calc-teaser.liquid
  Ported from the "Arcane Flame Website Prototype" option-c.html:
    - CSS: search by class name (`.calc`, `.steps`, `.ui`, `.ui__bar`,
      `.ui__body`, `.drop`, `.frow`, `.total` and their children) plus the
      .calc-relevant slice of the shared <=1080px responsive rule
      (`.hero__in,.craft,.calc{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:52px}`) and
      the <=680px `.total .amt{font-size:34px}` rule — see
      shopify-theme/assets/home-calc-teaser.css for the full colour-
      substitution notes.
    - Markup: `<section class="sec" id="calculator">...</section>` — the
      "No emails. No waiting." copy block with its 3-step list and CTA,
      plus the fake browser-chrome mockup of the calculator tool (URL bar,
      drop-zone, 3 example file rows, running total).

  Heading, lede, the 3 steps and the CTA text/url are section
  settings/blocks so a merchant can edit them without a theme code
  deploy. The browser-chrome mockup (URL bar text, drop-zone copy, the
  three example file rows with their names/specs/prices, the running
  total and the "spend & save" note) is hardcoded directly in this file,
  not exposed as settings — same reasoning as home-services.liquid's
  hardcoded "Uploaded STL / not a stock model" badge: this is decorative
  illustrative UI chrome demonstrating what the real tool looks like, not
  real order data, and letting a merchant "edit" fake file names/prices
  would invite something that reads as a genuine price quote rather than
  a mockup.

  Judgment call — eyebrow: the brief's literal schema list is heading /
  lede / step blocks / CTA. Added an `eyebrow` text setting (source:
  "Instant quote calculator") anyway, matching the precedent set by
  home-craft.liquid and home-services.liquid (both of which also added an
  eyebrow setting beyond a brief's literal field list) — dropping it would
  lose real, obviously-editable copy for no reason. Flagged here and in
  the task report.

  Judgment call — heading line break: the source's h2 hard-breaks across
  two lines ("No emails.<br />No waiting.") purely for line-length
  balance, no semantic two-tone meaning. Modelled as a single plain
  `heading` text setting per the brief's literal field list (matching
  home-craft.liquid's choice for its own similar break) and left to wrap
  naturally; the manual break is dropped rather than smuggling markup
  into a single-line text field. Flagged in the task report.

  Judgment call — CTA URL: the source's CTA is `<a href="#">` (a dead
  link even within the prototype's own single-page anchor system for
  this button). This section is a homepage teaser; the actual working
  calculator lives on its own real page. Per the task brief, the `url`
  setting's default is set to the confirmed live calculator page path
  (`/pages/3d-print-calculator` — see docs/shopify-integration-runbook.md
  §2, "Calculator page" row) as a plain path string, not a
  `{{ pages.*.url }}` Liquid object reference — Shopify schema defaults
  are static JSON with no Liquid evaluation, so an object reference isn't
  valid there in the first place, and it also matches every other `url`
  setting already shipped in this section set (home-hero.liquid,
  home-final-cta.liquid, home-services.liquid), none of which use a
  `pages.*.url` object anywhere, in a default or otherwise. See task
  report for the full comparison.

  Judgment call — count-up total: the source animates `.total .amt` from
  £0.00 up to a hardcoded `TARGET = 39.95` via IntersectionObserver +
  requestAnimationFrame when the mockup scrolls into view (note: £39.95
  does not equal the sum of the three visible example rows, £47.00 — a
  quirk already present in the source, not introduced by this port).
  Consistent with every other section in this set (see
  home-final-cta.css's note on `.reveal`), no scroll-triggered animation
  JS has been ported anywhere in this theme; the final total is rendered
  as static markup showing the source's animation target, £39.95, and the
  `.reveal`/`data-d` classes are kept as inert scaffolding for parity.
{% endcomment %}
<section class="sec" id="Calc-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="calc">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2 class="display reveal" data-d="1">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        <div class="lede reveal" data-d="2">{{ section.settings.lede }}</div>
        <ol class="steps reveal" data-d="2">
          {% for block in section.blocks %}
            {% if block.type == 'step' %}
              <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <b>{{ block.settings.number }}</b>
                <div>
                  <h4>{{ block.settings.title }}</h4>
                  <p>{{ block.settings.description }}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
        {% if section.settings.cta_text != blank %}
          <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url }}" class="btn btn--primary reveal" data-d="3" style="margin-top:34px">
            {{ section.settings.cta_text }} <span class="arw">→</span>
          </a>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {% comment %} Decorative browser-chrome mockup — hardcoded, see file header. {% endcomment %}
      <div class="ui reveal" data-d="1" id="Calc-ui-{{ section.id }}">
        <div class="ui__bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>arcane-flame.com/pages/3d-print-calculator</span></div>
        <div class="ui__body">
          <div class="drop">
            <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><path d="m7 10 5-5 5 5"/><path d="M12 5v13"/></svg>
            <p>Drop your STL files here</p>
            <small>binary &amp; ASCII .stl · multi-part supported</small>
          </div>

          <div class="frow">
            <div class="frow__ico"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"/><path d="m2 17 10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg></div>
            <div class="frow__meta"><b>barbarian-hero.stl</b><small>32mm · resin · grey primer</small></div>
            <div class="frow__price">£8.40</div>
          </div>
          <div class="frow">
            <div class="frow__ico"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"/><path d="m2 17 10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg></div>
            <div class="frow__meta"><b>ruined-tower-terrain.stl</b><small>184mm · PLA · dark grey</small></div>
            <div class="frow__price">£21.60</div>
          </div>
          <div class="frow">
            <div class="frow__ico"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"/><path d="m2 17 10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg></div>
            <div class="frow__meta"><b>dice-tower-parts.stl</b><small>multi-part · PLA · assembled</small></div>
            <div class="frow__price">£17.00</div>
          </div>

          <div class="total">
            <div><small>Order total</small><div class="amt">£39.95</div></div>
            <div class="save">15% spend &amp; save applied<br /><b>Free UK shipping unlocked</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

